    <briefdescription>
<para>Wraps optional OCR processing for scanned image pages. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When THEMIS_ENABLE_OCR is set at build time and a Tesseract installation is available at runtime, this extractor passes image data through OCR and wraps the resulting text as an OCR_IMAGE-modality <ref refid="structthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_sample" kindref="compound">TrainingSample</ref>. If OCR is unavailable the extractor compiles and links cleanly but <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_o_c_r_extractor_1a5549866f18ca6471b7737bafee77a86f" kindref="member">isAvailable()</ref></computeroutput> returns <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_o_c_r_extractor_1aa02e98d0be278712a0a25e62158bc92a" kindref="member">extract()</ref></computeroutput> returns an empty vector.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The <computeroutput>image_path</computeroutput> argument is the filesystem path to a TIFF, PNG, or JPEG image of a scanned page. Pass the originating document_id as the second argument so provenance can be traced back. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
